# Docker Compose reads this file only for ${VAR} interpolation (for example
# APSOR_PUBLIC_HOST, APSOR_STORAGE_BACKEND, and the APSOR_R2_* settings). It
# is not passed into the containers: provider credentials such as
# APSOR_DEEPSEEK_API_KEY and R2 keys must live in .secrets/*.env, which Compose
# mounts read-only (see secrets/README.md).
#
# Required only for AI answers and AI summaries. Leave empty to use the
# deterministic extractive summary fallback and disable agent answers. The
# Settings UI can store an encrypted key in the database instead; the database
# wins. This key is also the environment fallback for the DeepSeek web search
# and web fetch provider; Settings can select DeepSeek for either capability.
APSOR_DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
# Exa is an optional web search/fetch provider. Put EXA_API_KEY in the
# gitignored .secrets/exa.env file; the Settings UI can also store an encrypted
# key in the database. A database row always wins.
# EXA_API_KEY=
# Optional output caps. Agent turns need room for long tool arguments; short
# summary/extraction calls keep the smaller budget. Set the chat cap to 0 to
# disable it and let the provider decide the output limit.
# APSOR_DEEPSEEK_CHAT_MAX_TOKENS=20000
# APSOR_DEEPSEEK_MAX_TOKENS=1800

# Anthropic Claude models (optional). Put ANTHROPIC_API_KEY (or the
# APSOR_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY name) in .secrets/anthropic.env; a key stored on an
# active provider row in the Settings UI wins. Agent chat uses
# APSOR_CHAT_AGENT_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS unless the row sets its own output cap.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# APSOR_ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-haiku-5-5
# APSOR_ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://api.anthropic.com
# APSOR_ANTHROPIC_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=120
# APSOR_ANTHROPIC_MAX_TOKENS=2000
# APSOR_ANTHROPIC_VERSION=2026-10-21
# APSOR_CHAT_AGENT_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS=64000
# Connection probes have their own short timeout, independent of chat calls.
# APSOR_CHAT_PROBE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=20

# Optional Fernet master key. When unset, data/.secret_key is created with 0600.
# APSOR_SECRET_KEY=

# Owner session cookie. Set true when served over HTTPS (Cloudflare compose does).
APSOR_COOKIE_SECURE=false
APSOR_SESSION_TTL_HOURS=720

# Storage. ``local`` keeps original bytes under APSOR_DATA_DIR; ``r2`` writes
# new originals to the private Cloudflare R2 bucket. Production sets r2 only
# after the storage migration has been verified. Keep local for development.
APSOR_STORAGE_BACKEND=local
# Non-secret R2 settings. The production Compose file defaults the bucket,
# region, and prefix. The account endpoint has no default: set it before
# running with the r2 backend.
# APSOR_R2_ENDPOINT_URL=https://<account-id>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
# APSOR_R2_BUCKET=apsor-archive
# APSOR_R2_REGION=auto
# APSOR_R2_PREFIX=
# R2 credentials belong in .secrets/r2.env (gitignored), not this file. The app
# also accepts the legacy unprefixed R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID / R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY
# names used by that local secret file. Container deployments mount .secrets
# read-only, and the file must be readable by uid 10001 (mode 644 or chown).
# APSOR_R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# APSOR_R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=

# Required by the production Caddy host matcher.
APSOR_PUBLIC_HOST=archive.example.com

# RabbitMQ ingest dispatch (optional). PostgreSQL ``file_ingest_job`` remains
# the authoritative job ledger: the broker only wakes a worker, redelivers
# unacked messages after a crash, and delays retries. With dispatch disabled or
# unavailable, the worker's one-second database polling drains the same jobs.
# The production Compose file sets this and a broker-internal URL itself. For a
# host-run API/worker with docker-compose.dev.yml, use:
#   APSOR_RABBITMQ_ENABLED=true
#   APSOR_RABBITMQ_URL=amqp://apsor:apsor@127.0.0.1:5672/
# Management UI: http://127.0.0.1:15672 (apsor / apsor). These are local demo
# credentials only; change RABBITMQ_DEFAULT_USER and RABBITMQ_DEFAULT_PASS
# before any shared or internet-reachable deployment. The app never logs the
# URL or credentials.
APSOR_RABBITMQ_ENABLED=false
# APSOR_RABBITMQ_URL=amqp://apsor:apsor@127.0.0.1:5672/
# APSOR_RABBITMQ_INGEST_EXCHANGE=apsor.ingest
# APSOR_RABBITMQ_INGEST_QUEUE=apsor.ingest.jobs
# APSOR_RABBITMQ_INGEST_RETRY_QUEUE=apsor.ingest.jobs.retry
# APSOR_RABBITMQ_CONNECT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=5
# Best-effort publish bound; an unreachable broker must not delay an upload.
# APSOR_RABBITMQ_PUBLISH_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=1
# APSOR_RABBITMQ_RETRY_TTL_MS=30000
# APSOR_RABBITMQ_MAX_DISPATCH_RETRIES=20
# Compose reads these two for the local broker container defaults.
# RABBITMQ_DEFAULT_USER=apsor
# RABBITMQ_DEFAULT_PASS=apsor

# Optional overrides.
# APSOR_DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://apsor:apsor@127.0.0.1:55432/apsor_archive
# APSOR_CACHE_URL=redis://127.0.0.1:56379/0
# APSOR_TIMEZONE=Asia/Taipei
# Tavily web fetch extraction depth: basic or advanced. Advanced is the default.
# APSOR_TAVILY_EXTRACT_DEPTH=advanced
# The HTTP client must outlast Tavily's advanced 30-second provider timeout.
# APSOR_WEB_FETCH_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=45
# APSOR_EMBEDDING_PROVIDER=openai
# APSOR_EMBEDDING_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# APSOR_EMBEDDING_MODEL=text-embedding-3-small
# APSOR_EMBEDDING_DIMENSION=1536
# APSOR_EMBEDDING_API_KEY=
